// [MULTI-HANDLE-MANY-LEXICAL] `many` relaxes the lexical `resume` rule of
// [EFFECTS-RESUME] exactly as far as its ground extends: a lambda CONSUMED
// before the arm returns may resume, because its continuation is still live
// (that accepted shape is `tests/regressions/effects/staged_multiplicity`).
// A lambda that ESCAPES the arm keeps the existing rejection — here it is
// handed to a spawned fiber, so it runs after the arm has already returned and
// its continuation is dead.
//
// TODAY the program is rejected twice: by the blanket [EFFECTS-RESUME] rule,
// and because `many` has no re-entrant continuation to offer any arm. The
// arm-naming wording [MULTI-HANDLE-MANY-LEXICAL] specifies arrives with phase 5
// of docs/plans/0028-resumption-multiplicity.md, which needs the multi-shot
// runtime of plan 0016; until then the blanket rule is not misleading, because
// no `many` arm compiles at all. This golden records what the compiler says,
// so the wording cannot change silently when that phase lands.
effect Choice {
    many pick: fn(int) -> int
}

fn search(seed) = perform Choice.pick(seed)

fn main() = {
    let picked = handle Choice
        pick option => {
            let escaping = |n| => resume((option + n) ?: option)
            let later = spawn escaping(1)
            option
        }
    in search(1)
    print("picked=${picked}")
}
